# Keep the Docker build context to what `cargo build --release` actually reads
# (Cargo manifests, crates/**, toolchain files). Anything else in the context
# invalidates the image layer cache on unrelated commits and forces a full
# release rebuild, which costs ~20 minutes per gate run.
.git
.github
.cursor
.claude
**/.DS_Store
**/node_modules
**/target
.artifacts
bench
models
pdfium
tessdata_best
vendor
web
plans
docs
# `app` cannot be excluded wholesale: the root Cargo.toml lists app/src-tauri as
# a workspace member, so `cargo build -p fileconv-server` fails to load the
# workspace without its manifest — and without its lib source too ("can't find
# library `fileconv_desktop_lib`"). Exclude the bulk of app/ (7.7 MB, mostly
# assets and icons) by path and leave Cargo.toml, build.rs and src/ (~180 KB) in
# the context. Listing paths rather than re-including with `!` keeps this
# independent of how a given builder treats exceptions inside an excluded
# directory.
app/assets
app/dist
app/node_modules
app/src
app/src-tauri/capabilities
app/src-tauri/fixtures
app/src-tauri/icons
app/src-tauri/native-runtime
app/src-tauri/target
tests
scripts
re-design
*.log
# Only the Dockerfiles are build inputs; compose files, env files, deploy
# scripts and service assets are runtime concerns and must not bust the cache.
# Keep the two embedding-cpu build inputs (COPY in Dockerfile.embedding-cpu).
deploy/compose*.yml
deploy/dev/**
!deploy/dev/requirements-embedding-server.txt
!deploy/dev/Dockerfile.embedding-cpu
deploy/spike
deploy/poc
deploy/backup
deploy/observability
deploy/scripts/**
!deploy/scripts/aiteamvn-embedding-server.py
deploy/README.md
deploy/.env
